      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. High-Performance Vector VRL Transform Pipeline</h2>
        <p>
          At enterprise scale (100k+ RPS per cluster), parsing logs with Logstash or Python is cost-prohibitive due to memory bloat and regex backtracking. <strong>Vector</strong> (built by Datadog in Rust) provides <strong>Vector Remap Language (VRL)</strong>, which executes structured parsing in sub-microsecond latency.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here is the complete, production-hardened VRL configuration:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-emerald-400">
# vector.yaml - Envoy Access Log Ingestion Pipeline
sources:
  envoy_logs:
    type: kubernetes_logs
    include_paths:
      - "/var/log/pods/*_envoy*/*.log"

transforms:
  parse_envoy:
    type: remap
    inputs:
      - envoy_logs
    source: |
      # Fast-path regex matching for default Envoy format
      parsed, err = parse_regex(.message, r'^\[(?P<timestamp>[^\]]+)\] "(?P<method>\S+) (?P<path>\S+) (?P<protocol>\S+)" (?P<status>\d+) (?P<flags>\S+) (?P<bytes_rx>\d+) (?P<bytes_tx>\d+) (?P<duration>\d+) (?P<upstream_duration>\S+) "(?P<x_forwarded_for>[^"]*)" "(?P<user_agent>[^"]*)" "(?P<request_id>[^"]*)" "(?P<authority>[^"]*)" "(?P<upstream_host>[^"]*)"$')
      
      if err != null {
        .parse_error = err
        .raw_payload = .message
      } else {
        # Cast numeric fields
        .timestamp = parse_timestamp(parsed.timestamp, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%.fZ") ?? now()
        .http_method = parsed.method
        .http_path = parsed.path
        .http_protocol = parsed.protocol
        .http_status = to_int!(parsed.status)
        .response_flags = parsed.flags
        .bytes_received = to_int!(parsed.bytes_rx)
        .bytes_sent = to_int!(parsed.bytes_tx)
        .duration_ms = to_int!(parsed.duration)
        .upstream_duration_ms = to_int(parsed.upstream_duration) ?? null
        .client_ip = parsed.x_forwarded_for
        .user_agent = parsed.user_agent
        .request_id = parsed.request_id
        .authority = parsed.authority
        .upstream_host = parsed.upstream_host
        
        # Enrich with decoded flag semantics
        .flag_description = match .response_flags {
          "UH" => "No Healthy Upstream Host",
          "UF" => "Upstream Connection Failure",
          "UO" => "Upstream Overflow / Circuit Broken",
          "UT" => "Upstream Request Timeout",
          "DC" => "Downstream Connection Terminated",
          "NR" => "No Route Configured",
          "LH" => "Local Service Failed Health Check",
          "-" => "Normal Execution",
          _ => "Other Failure"
        }
        
        # Remove raw string to save egress bandwidth
        del(.message)
      }

sinks:
  otel_exporter:
    type: opentelemetry
    inputs:
      - parse_envoy
    endpoint: "otel-collector.monitoring.svc.cluster.local:4317"
    protocol: grpc
</pre>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Comprehensive Envoy Response Flag Decoder Matrix</h2>
        <p>
          The <code>%RESPONSE_FLAGS%</code> field is Envoy’s most valuable troubleshooting asset. It identifies why a request failed without requiring packet captures or code tracing:
        </p>

        <!-- Flags Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white font-semibold">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-slate-800">Flag Code</th>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-slate-800">Semantic Meaning</th>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-slate-800">Typical HTTP Code</th>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-slate-800">Root Cause Diagnostics</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/60 font-mono">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">UH</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">No Healthy Host</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">503 Service Unavailable</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">All pods in target service failed readiness probes.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-rose-400">UF</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">Upstream Connection Failure</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">503 Service Unavailable</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">TCP reset (RST), connection refused, or TLS handshake failure.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-purple-400">UO</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">Upstream Overflow</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">503 Service Unavailable</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">Envoy circuit breaker hit max pending requests / connections.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">UT</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">Upstream Timeout</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">504 Gateway Timeout</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">Backend exceeded route timeout before transmitting body.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-300">DC</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">Downstream Connection Termination</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-amber-400">499 / 200</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">Client browser or caller hung up before response completed.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">NR</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-white">No Route</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-amber-400">404 Not Found</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-sans text-xs">No matching virtual host or route prefix in Envoy RDS.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. OpenTelemetry (OTel) Semantic Convention Mapping</h2>
        <p>
          When funneling parsed Envoy logs into Grafana Loki, ClickHouse, or Datadog via the OpenTelemetry Collector, engineering teams should strictly conform to <strong>OpenTelemetry Semantic Conventions for HTTP Logs</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><code>http.request.method</code> &rarr; Maps to parsed <code>method</code> (e.g. "POST").</li>
          <li><code>url.path</code> &rarr; Maps to parsed <code>path</code> (e.g. "/checkout").</li>
          <li><code>http.response.status_code</code> &rarr; Maps to integer <code>status</code> (e.g. 503).</li>
          <li><code>network.protocol.name</code> &rarr; Extracted from <code>protocol</code> (e.g. "http").</li>
          <li><code>server.address</code> &rarr; Maps to parsed <code>authority</code> (e.g. "api.internal.net").</li>
          <li><code>client.address</code> &rarr; First element of <code>x_forwarded_for</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Standalone Python Test Harness: Regex Performance & Parsing Guardrails</h2>
        <p>
          Execute this diagnostic Python validation harness to verify your Grok expressions against boundary cases (IPv6 addresses, absent upstream headers, truncated paths):
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-emerald-400">
import re
from typing import Dict, Any, Optional

ENVOY_PATTERN = re.compile(
    r'^\[(?P<timestamp>[^\]]+)\] '
    r'"(?P<method>\S+) (?P<path>\S+) (?P<protocol>\S+)" '
    r'(?P<status>\d{3}) (?P<flags>\S+) (?P<bytes_rx>\d+) (?P<bytes_tx>\d+) '
    r'(?P<duration>\d+) (?P<upstream_duration>\S+) '
    r'"(?P<x_forwarded_for>[^"]*)" "(?P<user_agent>[^"]*)" '
    r'"(?P<request_id>[^"]*)" "(?P<authority>[^"]*)" "(?P<upstream_host>[^"]*)"$'
)

def parse_envoy_line(line: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:
    match = ENVOY_PATTERN.match(line.strip())
    if not match:
        return None
    data = match.groupdict()
    return {
        "timestamp": data["timestamp"],
        "method": data["method"],
        "path": data["path"],
        "protocol": data["protocol"],
        "status": int(data["status"]),
        "flags": data["flags"],
        "duration_ms": int(data["duration"]),
        "upstream_host": data["upstream_host"]
    }

if __name__ == "__main__":
    test_line = (
        '[2026-10-05T08:14:22.412Z] "POST /api/v2/checkout HTTP/1.1" '
        '503 UH 1420 284 18 12 "203.0.113.19" "Mozilla/5.0" '
        '"a8f9c2d1" "api.internal.net" "10.244.3.18:8080"'
    )
    result = parse_envoy_line(test_line)
    assert result is not None, "Failed to parse standard Envoy log line"
    print("Parsed Record:", result)
</pre>
